    {
      "hash": "#2",
      "title": "Knee Imaging Background",
      "section": "main",
      "visuals": 2,
      "visibleText": "Radiographs are accessible but collapse depth. CT resolves 3D anatomy but adds cost and radiation. This project reconstructs femur, tibia, patella and fibula from AP and lateral views.",
      "titleWords": 3,
      "narrativeWords": 28,
      "states": [
        {
          "activePanels": 0,
          "innerOverflow": false,
          "titleLines": 1,
          "stageStates": []
        }
      ],
      "fileName": "02.png"
    },
    {
      "hash": "#3",
      "title": "Reconstruction Problem Statement",
      "section": "main",
      "visuals": 3,
      "visibleText": "Many 3D shapes can explain the same two projections. Bone boundaries obscure one another in radiographs. A plausible smooth knee may still erase clinically important morphology.",
      "titleWords": 3,
      "narrativeWords": 26,
      "states": [
        {
          "activePanels": 0,
          "innerOverflow": false,
          "titleLines": 1,
          "stageStates": []
        }
      ],
      "fileName": "03.png"
    },
    {
      "hash": "#4",
      "title": "Medical Reconstruction Literature",
      "section": "main",
      "visuals": 1,
      "visibleText": "The field progressed from shape fitting to learned biplanar reconstruction. Comparisons remain difficult when studies change data, geometry and architecture together.",
      "titleWords": 3,
      "narrativeWords": 21,
      "states": [
        {
          "activePanels": 0,
          "innerOverflow": false,
          "titleLines": 1,
          "stageStates": []
        }
      ],
      "fileName": "04.png"
    },
    {
      "hash": "#5",
      "title": "Identified Research Gap",
      "section": "main",
      "visuals": 2,
      "visibleText": "Architecture, data, projection geometry and training often change together, obscuring the cause of improvement. Average overlap can conceal missing small bones, fold instability and subgroup failure.",
      "titleWords": 3,
      "narrativeWords": 26,
      "states": [
        {
          "activePanels": 0,
          "innerOverflow": false,
